meta {
  name: Get Family Attributes Collection
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e/attributes
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 and 2026-09-21 against the real pre-existing "Accessories"
  product family (id `6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e`) on "David's Dev Account" -- read-only
  `GET`, safe against real data.

  ## GET collection: /product-families/{id}/attributes
  New in the 2026-09-15 `openapi_pimv3.json` refresh. Lists every attribute currently
  linked to that family, scoped automatically by the path's `product_family_id` (unlike
  the top-level `GET /family-attributes`, this nested collection endpoint is correctly
  scoped -- no cross-tenant leak observed here).

  No pagination wrapper observed on this nested collection (25 entries returned in one
  page for "Accessories" with no `next_page`). The spec declares this operation's
  response schema as a bare empty `{}` -- no output DTO reference at all, unlike almost
  every other list endpoint in the spec. Treat the shape confirmed here as ground truth
  over the spec.

  ## GET by ID: /product-families/{id}/attributes/{attribute_id}
  New in the 2026-09-15 refresh. Fetches a single family<->attribute link record by both
  path segments.

  ## Key fields (both views)
  Each record: `account_id`, `level` (`"parent_level"` / `"no_level"` / `null`),
  `product_family_id`, `attribute_id`.

  ## Subpath discovery on the family root resource
  `GET /product-families/{id}/bogus_xyz` -- `400 {"errors":[{"name":"ValueError",
  "description":"Field 'bogus_xyz' not found. Available fields: ['id','account_id',
  'name','total_products','total_attributes','total_models','created','modified']"}]}`
  -- matches `ProductFamilyOutputDto` exactly, no undocumented internal fields (same
  clean pattern as `product-categories`/`relationships`, unlike products/assets).
}

example {
  name: Get Family Attributes Collection - Success
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 against the real "Accessories" product family, trimmed to 3 of 25 entries (full response has no pagination and returns all 25 at once).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-families/6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e/attributes
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "no_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19b1"},
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19b2"},
            {"account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c", "level": "parent_level", "product_family_id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b186e", "attribute_id": "6a38f613c3d65a5f868b19b3"}
          ],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

